msgid "Slots"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Where a command of a plugin appears, what EMStudio gives it, and what it"
" gives back.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A **slot** is a place of the interface, or of the work, where EMStudio "
"accepts something from a plugin. It has a name and a version, "
"``context.node@1``, a promise the program keeps from one release to the "
"next. A command lists its slots in ``in``; a slot with a version higher "
"than the program knows turns that entry off, not the plugin, and the "
"Extensions page says so."
msgstr ""

msgid "The slots of this version"
msgstr ""

msgid "Slot"
msgstr ""

msgid "Where it appears"
msgstr ""

msgid "What the command is"
msgstr ""

msgid "``menu.tools@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``Tools ▸ Plugins``, under the name of the plugin"
msgstr ""

msgid "a command"
msgstr ""

msgid "``menu.file.import@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``File ▸ Import``"
msgstr "``Datei ▸ Importieren``"

msgid "``menu.file.export@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``File ▸ Export``; the command returns a file"
msgstr ""

msgid "returns a file"
msgstr ""

msgid "``export.narrative@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Export ▾** of the Narrative; the command returns a file"
msgstr ""

msgid "``context.node@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "the context menu of a node, in the Matrix and in the Space"
msgstr ""

msgid "``door.reader@2``"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Porta dentro…*: a reader of a kind of file, or of a folder"
msgstr ""

msgid "``check@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "the **Warnings** sheet of the Tabular window: warnings"
msgstr ""

msgid "reads only"
msgstr ""

msgid "``event@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "no place: the plugin listens to an event (``ctx.on``)"
msgstr ""

msgid "a call of the API"
msgstr ""

msgid "``space.pick@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "no place: the plugin asks for a point (``em.app.space.pick``)"
msgstr ""

msgid "``console@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "no place: functions for the console (``em.ext.<id>``)"
msgstr ""

msgid "``inspector.section@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "a section of the Inspector, for some types of node"
msgstr ""

msgid "``tabular.column@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "a computed column of a sheet of the Tabular window"
msgstr ""

msgid "``statusbar@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "a short text in the status bar"
msgstr ""

msgid "``space.tool@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "a tool in the bar of the Space: what the person places"
msgstr ""

msgid "``panel@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "a panel declared in ``[[code.panels]]``"
msgstr ""

msgid "declared, not a command"
msgstr ""

msgid "``space.layer@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "a layer of the Space, drawn from what the command describes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Names reserved for later versions, accepted by the validator with a "
"warning and not drawn yet: ``context.outliner@1``, ``context.edge@1``, "
"``palette@1``, ``keymap@1``, ``workspace@1``."
msgstr ""

msgid "What a command receives"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A command is a function ``fn(slots)``. ``slots`` is a dictionary whose "
"keys are the ``name`` of each slot declared in ``[[code.commands]]``; "
"EMStudio fills them by their ``kind``, and **never invents a value**:"
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid "Kind"
msgstr "Art"

msgid "What EMStudio puts there"
msgstr ""

msgid "``id``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A selected node: the first ``id`` slot gets the first selected node, the "
"second the second. In a section of the Inspector, the node shown."
msgstr ""

msgid "``ids``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All the selected nodes, a list; in a column of the Tabular window, the "
"rows of the sheet."
msgstr ""

msgid "``path``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The file or folder of a reader, an import or a panel's field; for a "
"command of a menu whose ``path`` is required, EMStudio asks for a file "
"first (desktop only)."
msgstr ""

msgid "``geometry``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"What the person placed with a tool of the Space: the ``primitive``, its "
"``vertices`` in the frame of the model, the node it was placed ``on``, "
"the ``frame``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``string``, ``number``, ``bool``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"What the person wrote in the field of a panel of the same ``name``. Never"
" guessed: a required one that is missing refuses the command, with its "
"name."
msgstr ""

msgid "What a command gives back"
msgstr ""

msgid "What the function returns, and what EMStudio does with it"
msgstr ""

msgid "``menu.tools@1``, ``context.node@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Anything: a text is shown in a message, other values as JSON. A command "
"that wrote says how many steps it wrote."
msgstr ""

msgid "``menu.file.export@1``, ``export.narrative@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A file, ``ctx.file(name, content, mime)``: EMStudio saves it where the "
"person chooses (desktop) or downloads it (web)."
msgstr ""

msgid "``menu.file.import@1``, ``door.reader@2``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"What the reading wrote, inside ``em.write``. A reader declares ``accept``"
" (the extensions it takes, those EMStudio does not know), ``claims`` "
"(extensions EMStudio knows, offered as *Read as: …* beside its own "
"reading), ``folders = true`` (it reads a folder), and ``panel`` (a panel "
"of the plugin where the person says what the files do not)."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A list of warnings, each ``{\"rule\": …, \"sev\": \"error\" | \"warning\""
" | \"info\", \"node\": <id or None>, \"txt\": <text or {\"en\": …, "
"\"it\": …}>}``, shown in the **Warnings** sheet. It only reads."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Rows: a dictionary ``{label: value}``, a list of ``{\"label\", "
"\"value\"}`` or of pairs, or a text (one row). At most 40 rows of 200 "
"characters. It only reads; ``buttons`` names commands drawn under the "
"rows."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``{id: value}`` for the rows of the sheet named by ``view``, each at most"
" 200 characters. It only reads."
msgstr ""

msgid "One line, at most 80 characters. It only reads."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"What the tool wrote, inside ``em.write``. The command declares "
"``primitive`` and ``icon``, and a slot of kind ``geometry``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The description of a layer, ``layer = \"raster_stack\"``: planes with a "
"picture, which EMStudio draws. The pictures live in the plugin's own "
"folder. :doc:`/reference/geofisica` shows one at work."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A text may always be a dictionary of languages, ``{\"en\": \"…\", \"it\":"
" \"…\"}``: EMStudio shows the language of the interface, else English."
msgstr ""

msgid "Slots that are calls of the API"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Four slots need no command: the plugin uses them from ``setup(ctx)`` or "
"from a command."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``event@1`` — ``ctx.on(event, fn)``: ``fn(payload)`` runs after each "
"event of every study (the events are listed in :doc:`em-api`). A write in"
" a listener runs after the event, never inside the step that caused it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``space.pick@1`` — ``em.app.space.pick(prompt, primitive)`` asks the "
"person to place a point (or a line, a path, a surface) in the Space."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``console@1`` — ``ctx.expose(name, object)`` makes a function available "
"in the console as ``em.ext.<plugin>.<name>``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``panel@1`` — ``[[code.panels]]`` in the envelope (see :doc:`envelope`): "
"EMStudio draws the fields, the values computed by read-only commands, and"
" the buttons that run commands with the fields."
msgstr ""

msgid "Read only means read only"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A command in a slot that only shows a value (``check``, "
"``inspector.section``, ``tabular.column``, ``statusbar``, "
"``space.layer``) is declared ``writes = false``; one declared otherwise "
"is refused by the validator, and a write it attempts is refused by the "
"library."
msgstr ""

msgid "From the slots to «Where you will find it»"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Extensions page of the Settings tells the person, for every "
"extension, **where it will show** in EMStudio, under *Where you will find"
" it*. Nothing of that list is written by hand: EMStudio reads it from "
"your envelope, from the ``in`` of each command, from ``[[code.panels]]`` "
"and from the vocabularies of the data. What you declare is what the "
"person reads, before installing."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you declare"
msgstr ""

msgid "The line of *Where you will find it*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**File ▸ Bring in…**, *reader* and the command's label; with ``folders = "
"true``, *it reads a folder*"
msgstr ""

msgid "``menu.file.import@1``, ``menu.file.export@1``"
msgstr ""

msgid "**File ▸ Import**, **File ▸ Export**"
msgstr ""

msgid "``[[code.panels]]``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Right panel**, **Left panel**, **Panel below** or **A window of its "
"own**, from its ``place`` (right when it is not given), with the panel's "
"``label``"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Space ▸ Layers**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Space ▸ Tools**, every tool's label"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Inspector**, *section* and its label; **Show me** says the kind of node"
" to select (its ``when``)"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Tabular ▸ Columns**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Status bar**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Tools menu**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**A node's context menu**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Checks**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Narrative ▸ Export**"
msgstr "**Erzählung ▸ Exportieren**"

msgid "``[[data.vocabularies]]``"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Vocabularies**, *in the Inspector's pickers*, by name"
msgstr ""

msgid "any command"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Python**: the line that runs it from the console, "
"``em.plugins.invoke(\"<plugin>\", \"<command>\", {…})`` with its required"
" slots, for the first command that no menu carries (else the first), and "
"*+ N more commands*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The lines keep this order, one per place, whatever the order of your "
"commands; two commands in the same slot share one line, with both labels."
" A line is marked ● when the place is there now (the code loaded, the "
"data installed) and ○ when it comes with the code, and **Show me** takes "
"the person there."
msgstr ""

msgid "What this asks of an author:"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"give every command and every panel a ``label`` in the languages you can "
"(``{\"en\": …, \"it\": …}``): the line shows the label, else the id;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"declare the slots the command really serves: a command in no slot is "
"still reachable, but only from Python;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"declare ``folders = true`` on a reader that takes a folder, and ``place``"
" on a panel that should not open on the right."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The places are read from the archive before anything is installed (the "
"preview of **Install from disk…** and of a repository's **Install** says "
"them), so the person knows where to look before trusting your code."
msgstr ""

